(a) It shall be unlawful for any employee of the city to have on such employee's person, either concealed or unconcealed, or in such employee's immediate possession, or to bring onto any premises of the city any of the following implements:
(1) Any firearms, guns, pistols or other instruments of like kind or similar character;
(2) Any sword or dirk, spear or sword-in-a-cane;
(3) Any knife which has a blade that opens automatically by hand pressure applied to a button, spring or other device in the handle, the blade of which when open projects from the handle more than four inches;
(4) Any knife which has any obstruction or other device of any kind which holds the blade partly open, the blade of which when open projects from the handle more than four inches;
(5) Any knife of any kind, the blade of which when open projects from the handle more than three inches; this is intended to include all knives, such as butcher knives or other knives which do not close;
(6) Any straight razors;
(7) Any ice picks or similar device having a sharp point;
(8) Any knucks;
(9) Any explosives;
(10) Any articles or combination of articles likely to be made into so as to produce an explosive, including but not limited to gas, fire or water;
(11) Slingshots, bows and arrows, cannon, artillery or fireworks;
(12) Gas bombs, fire bombs, water bombs or similar type bombs or like in kind likely to produce harm either to the person or property of the city; or any or all other instruments, implements, objects or device that would or could produce harm or injury to any person or property of the city or of another.
(b) The following employees or special employees of the city are authorized to carry pistols or other weapons or equipment when such is lawfully issued to them:
(1) Police;
(2) Park police;
(3) Airport police;
(4) Security guards employed by the city;
(5) Court bailiffs;
(6) Probation officers;
(7) Special officers employed by the city;
(8) Specially deputized citizens or employees of the city;
(9) Personnel employed by the office of corrections.
(c) Any violation of this section or any subsection thereof shall be considered an offense and any person convicted of violating the terms of this section or any subsection thereof shall be subject to the penalties provided in section 1-8.
(Ord. of 1-21-03(2))
State Law reference— Carrying deadly weapons to or at public gatherings, O.C.G.A. § 16-11-127; concealed revolver of pistol licenses, O.C.G.A. § 16-11-128.

509:
(a) No person shall, after having been requested not to do so by a law enforcement officer, or any authorized agent of the property owner, park or stand on an unoccupied parking area or unoccupied motor vehicle in a parking area or repeatedly drive a motor vehicle through or within parking area located on privately owned property provided by a merchant, group of merchants, or shopping center or other facility for customer if:
(1) The parking area is identified by at least one sign as specified in this paragraph, or if the parking area contains more than 150 parking spaces, then by at least one such sign at each entrance to the parking area, each such sign containing the following information in easy to read printing:
a. Notice of this Code section;
b. Identification of the property which is reserved for customers use only;
c. Identification of the merchant, group of merchants, or shopping center or other similar facility providing the parking area; and
d. Warning that violators will be prosecuted.
(2) The motor vehicle is parked, is standing or is being operated other than for the purpose of:
a. Transporting some person to or from the interior of the place of business of a merchant identified by the sign in the parking area or to or from the interior of the shopping center or other facility so identified;
b. Making use of a telephone, vending machine, automatic teller, or other similar facility located in the parking area;
c. Meeting the requirements of a situation in which it has unexpectedly become impossible or impractical for the motor vehicle to continue to travel on the public roads; or
d. Carrying out any activity for which express permission has been given by the owner of the parking area or an authorized representative of the owner.
(b) Any person who violates subsection (a) of this Code section shall be guilty of a misdemeanor and, upon conviction thereof; shall be punished by a fine:
(1) Not to exceed $50.00 for the first such offense;
(2) Not to exceed $100.00 for the second such offense;
(3) Not to exceed $150.00 for the third subsequent such offense.
(c) The governing authority of any municipal corporation by ordinance may adopt by reference the provisions of subsection (a) of this Code section with out publishing or posting in full the provisions thereof. Any person violating any such ordinance shall be subject to a monetary fine:
(1) Not to exceed $50.00 for the first such violation;
(2) Not to exceed $100.00 for the second such violation; and
(3) Not to exceed $150.00 for the third or subsequent such violation.
Any vehicle that is parked on the sidewalk or on the wrong side of the roadway when designated for parking or any vehicle parked on the yellow curbing can be sited under this Code section for being improperly parked, this Code section will fall under rules of the road O.C.G.A. tit. 40 Motor Vehicle and Traffic.
(Ord. of 1-21-03(2))

